be a netrunner from the  start  didn't mean i couldn't level up and  invest in other skills and attributes  as i played i found myself more and more  reliant on stealth than i expected  most of the encounters would begin with  me hacking a character or the  environment  sneaking up on the distracted enemy and  either non-lethally choking them out or  violently snapping their neck  in almost every situation though i got  spotted and cleared out the remaining  enemies with my trusty pistol or a  grungy lead pipe i scavenged off a dead  gang member  so to recap each attribute is tied to  skill trees as you level up you'll get  attribute and perk points which can be  used to increase attributes and unlock  new perks respectively  you're not tied to a specific path or  playstyle but the attributes you invest  in will affect the perks you can unlock  in the early hours  like i said i more or less played as a  net runner a very bad net runner  and being a bad net runner meant that i  had to be ready with some iron just in  case things got hairy  usually i'd approach most situations by  hacking into an enemy this triggers a  hacking minigame that asks you to match  a sequence of numbers and letters on  your right with a bunch of letters and  numbers on your left  when you pick a number it locks you into  that row and you need to find the next  number or letter in the sequence  on that same row if you manage to find  that number or letter it will lock you  into the column and so on  it's a bit tough to explain but i  thought it was fun as hell could it be  gwent 2.0  i mean who knows what i can say is i  didn't think i'd be this excited to line  up numbers and hack stuff  once you are in the local mainframe you  can hack objects and characters in  different ways depending on your play  style  however you have to hack sparingly when  you first breach into the system  you are more or less given hacking  points everything you hack will eat into  those points  but of course my technical sleuthing  almost always ended with a  firefight complete with blood gore and  mayhem the myriad firearms i picked up  and messed around with were loud and  kicked like a donkey  this made gunfights feel weighty and  frantic as i ducked in and out of cover  based on the build i played the shooting  itself is serviceable  it's nowhere near as smooth as your  destinies or call of duties  but it was punchy and responsive when it  needed to be a generous aim assist pulls  your reticle to threats when you aim  down sights and headshots are rewarded  with a critical hit  indicator when i wasn't shooting enemies  i bashed them with a lead pipe the pipe  didn't quite have the same  thunderous impact that my firearms did  but it was fun charging threats and  thwacking them over the head whenever i  saw an opening  also deadly force isn't limited to  combat situations like in the witcher 3.  at the beginning of my demo i stabbed a  cop in a very gta fashion because i  wanted to see what would happen  night city pd promptly put out a warrant  for my arrest in the courtyard i was in  devolved into chaos  civvies were running around screaming  cars were honking and these hud was  constantly glitching in and out  i also hit some corporal guy with a pipe  because he told me to [ __ ] off  i regret nothing another big part of  cyberpunk's gameplay loop  are vehicles v owns a sporty quadrivitec  which they can call to their location  using the d-pad but you can also steal  parked cars with ease  stealing an npc controlled car though  requires a specific skill  as you'd expect cars handle differently  depending on their size  form factor and model these car felt  speedy and responsive making it easy to  weave between traffic and civilians  i also took a van for a test spin and  that felt sluggish and far less  responsive  as it should while vehicles were a  reliable way to get around the city i  actually found myself walking to most of  my objectives  the city is so dense and packed with  detail i was constantly getting  sidetracked the side alley would open up  into a bustling marketplace with food  vendors and shops  most of these areas were flanked with  colorful digital advertisements that  blared thumping music as i pushed my way  through the crowds  in one area i ran into a sidewalk  preacher yelling about how civilization  is doomed  after listening to his sermon for a bit  two young kish looking girls walked up  and started taking selfies with the  crazy street man  their words not mine the only reason i  didn't spend my entire demo aimlessly  wandering around night city was because  i had a time limit  now that i've gone over the gameplay  let's talk a bit about the quest in  cyberpunk  2077 like the witcher 3 there are many  different types of quests  all with recommended levels main quests  side quest gigs and incidental  activities that pop up on your map  if we use the witcher 3 as a base main  quest and side quest should be pretty  self-explanatory  gigs felt like they could be similar to  monster contracts and that they are  mostly self-contained stories that won't  affect the greater narrative in any big  ways  to be honest i actually didn't see too  many quests in my demo  most of the story quests i was able to  play we had already  seen however i did play a lot of these  incidental world events that reminded me  a lot of random encounters that you  might find in red dead redemption 2.  these usually consisted of clearing out  his own overrun by gangsters subduing  characters with warrants out on them and  looting caches  based on what i played these diversions  were pretty straightforward in theory  but  allowed for a lot of gameplay  experimentation with very little risk  in one section a gang had overrun a  small marketplace so  i hacked into the local mainframe  unfortunately i failed the hack and a  rival netrunner took notice  i think they set all my cybernetic  implants on fire but it was hard to tell  in the heat of the moment  all i know is that my screen turned  orange i couldn't heal and died  so i respawned and circled around the  marketplace to see if i could get them  from behind  i successfully hacked one gang member  and moved in slowly for some stealth  takedowns  but of course someone noticed me and a  lethal firefight broke out  while this specific instance may not  blow you away i'm really excited to see  how those combat encounters evolve and  develop as you build out your character  and unlock new skills and perks even  though i was early on i felt like the  game gave me plenty of options for  dealing with each encounter  so there's a look at the character  builder the combat the exploration  and the various events you will stumble  upon as you explore night city if you  enjoyed this video and want more  cyberpunk 2077 content we have our  impressions on the demo up now and a  brief story overview based on what we  know so far  and finally next week we will be doing a  q a video where we will answer your  questions about cyberpunk 2077  if you want to ask us something you can  leave us a comment below or you can find  me on twitter at jacob deck  see you next time you order  two tequila fashions with a splash of  service and a chili garnish  duo of johnny silverhands coming up  you

